  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.4. Increased capacity of member States and enterprises to develop policies and measures that promote the alignment of business practices with decent work and a human-centred approach to the future of work</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The national focal points designated in accordance with annex II of the ILO MNE Declaration and located in the Ministry of Labour and Social Security (MLSS), the Sierra Leone Local Content Agency, and in employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations developed an action plan, which includes capacity building, research and advocacy activities. Key milestones of this action plan were implemented by the national constituents:  the promotion of the MNE Declaration mainstreamed in the Sierra Leone Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) Investment Plan (Ministry of Planning and Economic Development); an MNE Unit has been created in the Ministry of Labour and Social Security (MLSS) with the main objective of promoting social dialogue between employees, employers, government and MNEs in order to enhance decent job creation and improve local economic development). The activities to promote the ILO MNE Declaration were included in 2022 Annual budget of the MOLSS. A Technical Working Group  to coordinate actions for the promotion of the MNE Declaration in Sierra Leone was created and inaugurated in September 2021. The Technical Working group comprises of national institutions including the Ministries of Finance, Information and Communication, Technical and Higher Education, Trade &amp; Industry, Mines and Mineral Resources, Local Government &amp; Rural Development, the Office of the Chief Minister at State House, Bank of Sierra Leone, National Revenue Authority, and National Youth Commission under the leadership of the MLSS.The national focal point of the Local Content Agency (SLLCA) has taken steps to engage 29 enterprises in the country on the application of the principles of the MNE Declaration. The national focal point from the MNE Focal Person at the Sierra Leone Labour Congress (SLLC) created a Trade Union Network on multinational enterprises made of 6 different trade unions. Members have been trained on the principles of the MNE Declaration. The ILO provided assistance to the national focal points for the promotion of the MNE Declaration in their efforts to promote the Declaration and the application of its principles in Sierra Leone. The ILO supported the focal points in their efforts to collect data on specific sectors where multinational enterprises operate through a study on the creation of more and decent jobs through multinational enterprises&#x2019; operations and their value chains in Sierra Leone focusing on the mining, banking, telecommunications and agribusiness sectors. The ILO will organize a capacity building activity for the members of the new Technical Working Group for the promotion of the MNE Declaration before the end of 2021.</narrative>
   </description>
